{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 20.66,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct review — the driver profile establishes a repeat deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d = 3) and this trip's deviation is material and substantiated on its own trace; the driver's conduct is referred for review. This referral rides with the monetary ruling and neither displaces nor delays it."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. Trip TRP-02827 ran on 29 Aug 2026 from Blk 108 Yishun Ring Rd to Blk 112 Ang Mo Kio Ave 4. The platform's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-02827) records the distance driven as 14.4 km against a booked optimal of 9.0 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02827). That is an excess of 5.4 km, or 60.0% of optimal. THE DEVIATION IS ESTABLISHED. POL-RD-01 measures actual distance from the trace, not the receipt copy, and both tests pass: 5.4 km exceeds 0.8 km and 60.0% exceeds 20%. Above 50% it is also a MATERIAL deviation. The trace is sound for policy purposes: 114 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, maximum gap 0.0 seconds, so none of POL-RD-07(a)–(c) is met, no independent corroboration is required and POL-RD-10(3) does not fire. NOTHING EXCUSES THE EXCESS. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02827) holds no messages, so no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04; the amendment fields on EV-TRIP-02827 are all null, so no relocation re-bases the route under POL-RD-05; the vehicle is RYDE_X, so the pooled baseline under POL-RD-12 does not apply. The driver's explanation, 'Road works.', has no advisory behind it: the bundle's only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-02827-01, is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) — no advisory covers this corridor in this window. POL-RD-03 therefore cannot be run, and under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13(2) the assertion carries no weight and the deviation stands at the measured figure. Because the driver named no advisory identifier, POL-RD-13(1) keeps this out of POL-RD-10(5), so the case does not escalate on that ground. THE MONEY. The driver's POL-RD-02 arithmetic is correct as far as it goes. charged_total: SGD 20.66 (EV-FARE-02827). recomputed_fare: SGD 14.99 — (3.80 base + 0.75 x 9.0 km + 0.28 x 13.0 min) x the 1.0 surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, plus the 0.80 platform fee. POL-RD-02 refund: SGD 5.70 (20.66 - 14.99 = 5.67, rounded up to the nearest 0.05). But POL-RD-06 applies whenever POL-RD-01 records a MATERIAL deviation, and this one is material. The driver profile (EV-DPROF-02827) shows deviation_flags_90d = 3, which meets the clause's '3 or more' limb and ESTABLISHES a repeat-deviation pattern. The argument that the ratio limb fails (3/180 = 0.0167) does not help: the clause is disjunctive and either limb establishes the pattern, so the ratio is not required. Limb (b) then applies because this deviation is both MATERIAL and substantiated on this trip's own trace. Side by side, as the clause requires: under POL-RD-02 alone SGD 5.70; under the POL-RD-06(b) uplift SGD 20.66, the whole of charged_total. There are no pass-through lines to carve out — tolls/ERP 0.00, airport surcharge 0.00, itemised gantry list empty — so the full charged_total is refunded. The uplift changes the remedy, not the finding: the deviation is found on this trip's trace alone under POL-RD-01, and the history is used only as POL-RD-06 and POL-GEN-01 permit — deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only and grounded nothing. The rider's claim for the whole fare is granted, but not by the route first put forward: POL-RD-02 alone caps the refund at 5.70 and the 90% full-refund share is not reached (5.67 is 27.4% of 20.66); the full refund comes from POL-RD-06(b). No billing-integrity correction arises: the ledger lines reconcile and no gantry or surcharge line is unmatched. No driver compensation is due — the billed 14.4 km is not less than the traced distance, so POL-RD-04's compensation limb gives nothing. Confidence is 0.90: every artifact deciding the case (EV-GPS-02827, EV-TRIP-02827, EV-FARE-02827, EV-DPROF-02827) carries weight 1.0, and the only zero-weight artifact, the missing advisory, carries no fact. The monetary effect (SGD 20.66) exceeds the POL-GEN-05 automatic execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so the amount is issued but held for release in the human queue; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 20.66,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c): refer driver DRV-09827 to driver-conduct review — a repeat deviation pattern is established (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 3 against 180 completed trips in the trailing 90 days). This referral rides with the monetary ruling and neither displaces nor delays it."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the arithmetic and the tribunal adopts it. The governing distance is the GPS trace, EV-GPS-02827 (weight_multiplier 1.0): trace_distance_km 14.4 km against the booked optimal of 9.0 km on the trip record, EV-TRIP-02827 (weight 1.0). That is an excess of 5.4 km, 60.0% of optimal, so both POL-RD-01 limbs pass (60.0% > 20% and 5.4 km > 0.8 km) and the 50% materiality gate is also cleared. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes: 114 fixes at the 10 s interval, 100.0% coverage, max_gap_sec 0.0, so POL-RD-07(a)–(c) is not met and the POL-RD-10(3) escalation does not open.\n\nNothing in the bundle excuses the excess, and both sides' own claims say so. EV-CHAT-02827 carries 0 messages, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable and no waypoint_hint exists for its 200 m test. pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at, amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min are all null on EV-TRIP-02827, so POL-RD-05 cannot be run. vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. fare_model is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-11 does not apply and POL-RD-02 governs. The bundle's only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-02827-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT (BLOCKING), so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and the driver's counterparty statement 'Road works.' is an assertion citing no evidence ID: under POL-RD-08 it discharges nothing, and under POL-RD-13(2) it neither reduces the excess nor supplies an amended optimal. Because the driver named no advisory evidence ID, POL-RD-13(1) keeps this out of POL-RD-10(5) — an assertion citing no artifact cannot be invoked against one — and no escalation trigger fires.\n\nPOL-RD-02 recomputation, read off EV-FARE-02827: recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 9.0 optimal km + 0.28 x 13.0 optimal min) x 1.0 surge, the multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier on EV-FARE-02827, + 0.80 platform fee, no ERP, no fixed surcharge, no waiting-time fee, no promo discount = 14.99. charged_total = 20.66. Refund = 20.66 - 14.99 = 5.67, rounded up to the nearest 0.05 = 5.70. That is 27.4% of charged_total, above the 0.50 de minimis floor and far below the 90% full-refund share, so POL-RD-02 alone yields PARTIAL_REFUND 5.70. The rider's demand for the entire fare is not available under POL-RD-02 by itself.\n\nThe larger sum comes from POL-RD-06. The deviation is MATERIAL, so the driver_profile check is required. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 3 satisfies that clause's first limb ('3 or more') outright; the ratio limb is an alternative, and its failure (3 / 180 = 0.0167) does not defeat the first. A repeat pattern is therefore ESTABLISHED. Side by side, as the clause requires: the POL-RD-02 figure is 5.70, and the POL-RD-06(b) uplifted figure is charged_total, 20.66. Limb (b) applies because this trip's deviation is both MATERIAL and substantiated on its own trace, so the remedy is FULL_REFUND of charged_total rather than the partial. The uplift is a remedy uplift only — the finding of deviation rests on POL-RD-01 evidence for this trip alone, never on the driver's history — and the driver's argument that the uplift is discretionary and defeated by the ratio test is rejected for the reasons just given. No pass-through line escapes the uplift: tolls_erp is 0.00, airport_surcharge is 0.00, erp_gantries is empty and the ledger reconciles to 20.66, so POL-RD-09 has nothing to settle separately and no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity finding arises. The whole contested 20.66 moves.\n\nThe profile field prior_deviation_flags is context-only under POL-GEN-01; both sides mentioned it only to disclaim it, so nothing is built on it and neither claim is discarded on that ground. The refund of 20.66 exceeds the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of 8.00, so it issues but is not executed automatically: the amount is held and placed in the human queue for release. Each party may appeal under POL-GEN-04.",
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c): refer driver DRV-09827 to driver-conduct review — a repeat deviation pattern is established (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 3 against 180 completed trips in the trailing 90 days). This referral rides with the monetary ruling and neither displaces nor delays it."
    ]
  },
